The timer is set for the end of the turn's request as if the turn on lent time were paid by its own units.
It lets pass the count at which the lender's units have paid for the request, and the borrower runs on unpaid.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: the timer lets the end of the turn's request pass
Witness: fuzz lend-payer-goes

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -385,7 +385,7 @@ static uint64_t turn_vtime(const struct core *core, const struct place *p, uint6
 /* The count the turn's request is over at, as its payer's units pay for the rest of it; COUNT_NEVER with none open. */
 static uint64_t turn_request_end(const struct core *core)
 {
-    const struct place *p = turn_place(core), *own = turn_own(core);
+    const struct place *p = turn_own(core), *own = turn_own(core);
     if (p == NULL || own == NULL || place_units(p) == 0 || !request_open(p, own)) {
         return COUNT_NEVER;
     }
